## 4. Recruiters Endpoint — `/api/recruiters/`

| Method   | Full URL             | Backend Action          | Hook in `useApi.ts`       |
|----------|----------------------|-------------------------|---------------------------|
| `GET`    | `/api/recruiters/`   | List all recruiters     | `useRecruiters()`         |
| `POST`   | `/api/recruiters/`   | Create recruiter        | `useCreateRecruiter()`    |

### Frontend Pages That Use This Endpoint

| Page File | Route | Hooks Used | Purpose |
|-----------|-------|------------|---------|
| `pages/LoginPage.tsx` | `/` (login dialog) | `useRecruiters()`, `useCreateRecruiter()` | Look up recruiter by email + password for login; create recruiter account on registration |

---

## 5. Custom Action — `/api/jobs/{id}/download_applications/`

| Method | URL | Backend Handler | Triggered From |
|--------|-----|-----------------|----------------|
| `GET`  | `/api/jobs/{jobId}/download_applications/` | `JobViewSet.download_applications()` | `RecruiterPostings.tsx` — "CSV" button via `window.open(...)` |

**What it returns:** A `text/csv` file with columns:  
`Name, SAP ID, Email, Department, 10th Score, 12th Score, CGPA, Resume URL, Custom Resume URL, Cover Note, Status, Applied At`

**Code location:** `backend/placements/views.py` — lines 45–72

---

## 6. External Service — ATS Resume Ranker

| Method | URL | Triggered From |
|--------|-----|----------------|
| `POST` | `http://127.0.0.1:8081/api/rank` | `RecruiterPostings.tsx` — "Analyze & Rank Top 10" button |

**This is NOT a Django route.** It calls a separate Python service running on port **8081** (the `CV-ATS-Checker` microservice in the repo).

**Payload:** `FormData` with:
- `job_description_file` — uploaded PDF/DOCX of the JD
- `applicants` — JSON array of `{ id, name, resumeUrl }`

**Response:** `{ rankings: [{ id, score, ... }] }` — sorted by ATS match score.

**Code location:** `placement-connect/src/pages/recruiter/RecruiterPostings.tsx` — lines 21–59

---

## 7. Coordinator Auth — `public/coordinators.csv`

Coordinators do **not** authenticate via the API. Instead, login reads a static CSV file served from `/coordinators.csv`:

| CSV Column | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| `Name` | Display name shown after login |
| `SAP ID` | Used as the login identifier |
| `Access Password` | Compared against entered password |

**File location:** `placement-connect/public/coordinators.csv`  
**Read in:** `pages/LoginPage.tsx` — lines 93–124 (via `fetch('/coordinators.csv')`)

---

## Complete Hook to Backend Route Summary

| Hook | HTTP Method | Backend Route | Django ViewSet |
|------|-------------|---------------|----------------|
| `useStudents()` | GET | `/api/students/` | `StudentViewSet.list` |
| `useCreateStudent()` | POST | `/api/students/` | `StudentViewSet.create` |
| `useUpdateStudent()` | PATCH / PUT | `/api/students/{id}/` | `StudentViewSet.partial_update / update` |
| `useJobs()` | GET | `/api/jobs/` | `JobViewSet.list` |
| `useCreateJob()` | POST | `/api/jobs/` | `JobViewSet.perform_create` (+ email side-effect) |
| `useApplications()` | GET | `/api/applications/` | `ApplicationViewSet.list` |
| `useCreateApplication()` | POST | `/api/applications/` | `ApplicationViewSet.create` |
| `useUpdateApplication()` | PATCH | `/api/applications/{id}/` | `ApplicationViewSet.partial_update` |
| `useRecruiters()` | GET | `/api/recruiters/` | `RecruiterViewSet.list` |
| `useCreateRecruiter()` | POST | `/api/recruiters/` | `RecruiterViewSet.create` |
| *(direct window.open)* | GET | `/api/jobs/{id}/download_applications/` | `JobViewSet.download_applications` |
| *(direct fetch)* | POST | `http://127.0.0.1:8081/api/rank` | External ATS service |

---

## Notes

- All data fetching uses **React Query** — results are cached by `queryKey` and automatically invalidated after mutations (`onSuccess`).
- There is **no authentication middleware** on the backend routes. Access control is entirely client-side via `AuthContext` + `localStorage`.
- `StudentViewSet` and `JobViewSet` use `MultiPartParser` + `FormParser` in addition to `JSONParser` to support file uploads (resumes, JD PDFs) via Cloudinary.
- Serializers apply a `_to_https()` helper on Cloudinary URLs (`resumeUrl`, `jdPdf`, `customResume`) to ensure HTTPS before sending to the frontend.
